## Initial closing obligation

Proposed lemma: every sufficiently large triangle-free global minimizer has a
same-label planar unit-separated placement that is nonexpansive on every pair
and strictly shortens every actual diameter pair.

`proposed lemma -> strict sub-D(n) same-cardinality competitor -> Level I`.

The unproved bridge was the simultaneous finite endpoint, not an infinitesimal
motion. The finite rhombus theorem below obstructs this transformation whenever
one old diameter pair is carried by an edge-connected unit-rhombus complex.

## Disposition

The general endpoint lemma is **not proved**. A stronger version based only on
triangle-freeness, optimal leading population, and normalized PSD KKT stress is
**rejected** by the explicit dense frame family. Its members are nonglobal.
The finite locking theorem, the full-source contact-preserving frame bow,
and exact regressions are preserved in
`docs/reports/seed090_finite_rhombus_contraction_2026-10-13.md`.
Level I and the canonical theorem frontier remain open and unchanged.

